I'm at 30% or so on NAO; I did quite a bit better in devnull but that also
included a decent stroke of luck. I've only burned one AoLS in my past
ten ascensions, I guess, but I've had them be very helpful three times:

 1. An Arc game on Devnull that ended up giving me a hat trick with bells 
    on--- on the quest locate level I accidentally pasted a picture of the 
    map, which of course has a very large number of . in it. I walked away 
    from the keyboard, #prayed, and found that my AoLS had protected me.
    I proceeded to ascend (and have not pasted in E-  Elbereth since).
 
 2. An Astral where I was dealing with Pestilence and had a shot to jump to
    a useful position that would almost certainly go away in one turn. I was
    willing to spend a bunch of turns Ill to get to an altar only because I 
    was wearing AoLS in case of emergency; once I didn't have a good jump, of
    course, I cured my sickness.

 3. A fast ascension (well, for me; around 5h15min playtime, probably) where
    I kept hitting 20HP or so on Astral and could comfortably ignore it 
    rather than burn valuable turns and time (valuable since I was going for 
    first ascension in the June NAO tournament) since I wasn't afraid to 
    "die." 

Those later cases and others I am not thinking of aren't times where I needed
the amulet's _effect_, but times where the amulet's _insurance_ made me 
comfortably playing more aggressively and, I believe, correctly. 

